     QQ__IIFFRRAAWWMMAASSKK() returns a _q-specific bit mask for _q's combined integer and
     fractional data bits.

     QQ__IIFFVVAALLIIMMAASSKK() and QQ__IIFFVVAALLFFMMAASSKK() return _q-specific bit masks for the in‐
     teger and fractional bits of _q's combined integer and fractional data
     bits value, i.e., are applicable to the values returned by QQ__GGIIFFAABBSSVVAALL()
     and QQ__GGIIFFVVAALL().

     QQ__GGIIFFRRAAWW() returns _q's raw masked integer/fractional data bits.

     QQ__GGIIFFAABBSSVVAALL() and QQ__GGIIFFVVAALL() return the absolute and real values of _q's
     integer/fractional data bits respectively.

     QQ__SSIIFFVVAALL() sets _q's combined integer/fractional data bits to the value
     _i_f_v, whereas QQ__SSIIFFVVAALLSS() independently sets _q's integer and fractional
     data bits to the separate values _i_v and _f_v.

     All of those functions operate on the following data types: _s_8_q___t, _u_8_q___t,
     _s_1_6_q___t, _u_1_6_q___t, _s_3_2_q___t, _u_3_2_q___t, _s_6_4_q___t, and _u_6_4_q___t, which are referred to
     generically as _Q_T_Y_P_E.  The _I_T_Y_P_E refers to the stdint(7) integer types.

     For more details, see qmath(3).

